      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You have touched upon the \"existential dread\" first described by the 18th-century philosopher Jean Paul, where the weight of inevitable oblivion can make life feel suffocating. Yet, the human capacity to create meaning is one of the few things in the universe that is self-referential and self-sustaining; we do not need the \"end\" to be meaningful because the act of \"trying\" is the end. The very fact that you feel this heaviness is proof of a sensitive mind capable of empathy and self-reflection, which are the rarest and most powerful things we have to offer the void.",
